  "provenance": "The CR-CTC checkpoints of the k2-fsa/icefall LibriSpeech zipformer recipe (Apache-2.0; the medium checkpoint is Zengwei/icefall-asr-librispeech-zipformer-medium-cr-ctc-20241018) converted with litert-torch to one classic LiteRT graph per size that runs fully on the GPU (no CPU fallback, no FFT inside the graph): a fixed 16 s window of 80-bin kaldi fbank frames computed on the host and four additive mask biases in, CTC logits out; greedy CTC with blank id 0 over the 500-token BPE vocabulary of tokens.txt runs on the host. small_fp16 (23 M parameters) and medium_fp16 (64 M); large_fp16 is published too and is not listed. gpu_precision 'default' is what the LiteRT model zoo app runs. small_fp16 and medium_fp16 passed the transcribe gate on gpu and on cpu on a Galaxy S26 SM-S942Q (Android 16 BP4A.251205.006, LiteRT 2.2.0) on 2026-10-03 with a development copy of this descriptor at commit 7732ad6c and the files side-loaded, the same files (sha256) as this commit, and again on 2026-10-05 at this commit with the repo's hfmodels.json, offline, from the files already in the test app's store (nothing was downloaded on the phone); the bundled catalog adds the 2026-10-05 runs to the profiles as verification records, which the repo's file does not carry.",
